WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.720
The benchmark view reads seven compatible
representative artifacts from the earlier

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.870
reviewed study.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.793
Every row describes
the same four thousand,

00:00:09.793 --> 00:00:13.670
three hundred and fifty seven
observed validation hours.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.410
Opening the view or changing its
sort order fits no new model.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.020
The active saved predictor remains the
hour and working day mean chosen by the

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.750
overall mean absolute error objective.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.940
This distinction is useful because a
comparison table can change its visual

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.870
winner when the question changes.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.890
We keep the source scope,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.680
output policy and selected candidate
visible rather than treating the first

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.210
displayed row as an
implicit new deployment.

00:00:45.643 --> 00:00:50.453
Groups has overall mean absolute
error ninety one point five seven,

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:54.633
compared with ninety nine point
eight three for the retained forest.

00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:57.293
June reverses that comparison:

00:00:58.263 --> 00:00:59.533
groups is near one
hundred and forty three,

00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:03.093
while the forest is near
ninety point eight eight.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:08.953
Groups also has lower working day rush
error, although that error remains large.

00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:12.123
June contains seven hundred
and twenty observations,

00:01:12.123 --> 00:01:15.133
and the defined rush slice
seven hundred and fifty.

00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:20.013
The forest number belongs to
one seed seventeen artifact,

00:01:20.423 --> 00:01:23.053
not the earlier mean
across three fitting seeds.

00:01:23.543 --> 00:01:28.023
These values describe a real tradeoff
rather than one uniformly strongest

00:01:28.023 --> 00:01:28.953
function.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:36.167
The shown interface code copies the
retained rows and sorts them by either

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.517
June error or overall error.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:43.417
It changes rendering order, with no
call to fitting or candidate selection.

00:01:44.327 --> 00:01:48.317
Sorting by June puts the deep tree first,
followed by the forest.

00:01:48.927 --> 00:01:51.997
The group row still carries
its saved candidate badge.

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:57.547
Adopting a June only objective or a
different operational cost would require

00:01:57.547 --> 00:02:00.357
an explicit new comparison and decision.

00:02:01.007 --> 00:02:05.967
A user exploring the existing evidence
should not silently alter the function

00:02:05.967 --> 00:02:08.037
answering the next hourly request.

00:02:08.807 --> 00:02:12.517
That is why display state and
prediction state stay separate.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:19.607
The representative forest fitted locally
in about zero point six seven six seconds

00:02:19.607 --> 00:02:24.637
and saved sixteen million, eighty
seven thousand, six hundred JSON bytes.

00:02:25.307 --> 00:02:29.157
The group fit took about zero
point zero one three six seconds.

00:02:29.927 --> 00:02:33.537
These are retained observations from
that machine and implementation.

00:02:34.607 --> 00:02:36.577
JSON size measures storage,

00:02:37.007 --> 00:02:38.017
not peak memory.

00:02:38.447 --> 00:02:42.277
Batch replay timing measures
transparent saved state traversal,

00:02:42.427 --> 00:02:45.037
not optimized per request
production latency.

00:02:46.007 --> 00:02:49.217
A direct linear solve has
zero iterative updates,

00:02:49.547 --> 00:02:51.477
which does not mean it was never fitted.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:56.227
A null convergence field means that
particular iterative criterion was not

00:02:56.227 --> 00:02:56.797
applicable.

00:02:57.807 --> 00:03:01.297
The fitting details retain those
distinctions beside the quality numbers.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:07.757
The practical source study
reports zero failed main trials.

00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:12.817
Earlier excessive rate optimizer
failures remain in their own run records.

00:03:13.487 --> 00:03:17.887
We do not merge unrelated studies to
manufacture a different failure count,

00:03:17.887 --> 00:03:20.037
or hide those earlier results.

00:03:20.747 --> 00:03:25.567
The separate three pass Adam recovery
demonstration is not another ranked

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:26.857
validation candidate.

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:31.637
It verifies continuation rather
than improving the model choice.

00:03:32.627 --> 00:03:37.727
A working application and exact restart
make the project more usable and

00:03:37.727 --> 00:03:38.697
reproducible.

00:03:39.287 --> 00:03:41.977
They preserve the candidate’s
lack of month response,

00:03:42.447 --> 00:03:43.737
large commute deficits,

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.097
unmeasured inventory consequences

00:03:46.627 --> 00:03:48.457
and absent calibrated uncertainty.

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:52.477
None of those limits disappears
because the interface runs.

00:03:56.013 --> 00:03:57.103
One hundred and nine source checks,

00:03:57.173 --> 00:04:00.063
independent arithmetic
and artifact audits,

00:04:00.293 --> 00:04:04.003
installed package checks and
actual browser checks pass.

00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:07.783
The complete written records
preceded these section companions.

00:04:08.653 --> 00:04:13.353
That evidence establishes implemented
local behavior rather than the learner’s

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.683
own explanation or an
operator’s improved decisions.

00:04:17.453 --> 00:04:20.203
The application rejects
reserved test dates,

00:04:20.373 --> 00:04:22.443
preserving the later held out assessment.

00:04:23.193 --> 00:04:25.443
Hosted recovery remains unverified.

00:04:26.093 --> 00:04:27.363
Before advancing,

00:04:27.593 --> 00:04:33.103
explain how a short linear run can
recover perfectly yet still fit poorly,

00:04:33.513 --> 00:04:38.103
and how the saved group model can
win overall while missing June badly.

00:04:38.773 --> 00:04:41.103
Those questions connect reproducibility,

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:46.103
model quality and the objective instead
of treating them as one success condition.

